# Local Phoenix self-host environment for Phoenix Audit dev.
#
# When you `docker compose up -d` in this directory, Phoenix runs on:
#   http://localhost:6006  (UI + REST + OTLP-HTTP)
#
# To point Phoenix Audit's smoke scripts at this local Phoenix instead of
# Phoenix Cloud, set THESE env vars in your shell or in
# ~/.config/phoenix-rat/.env:
#
#   PHOENIX_API_KEY=<unused-locally-but-must-be-set>
#   PHOENIX_COLLECTOR_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:6006
#
# Verify it's up:
#   curl http://localhost:6006/healthz   # should return "ok"
#   open http://localhost:6006           # see the Phoenix UI

# For VPS deployment, add these env vars when launching docker compose:
#   PHOENIX_ENABLE_AUTH=true
#   PHOENIX_SECRET=<32+ char random string>
#   PHOENIX_DEFAULT_ADMIN_INITIAL_PASSWORD=<secure password>
# Then expose 6006 behind nginx + TLS. Do NOT expose 4317 (OTLP gRPC) publicly.
